                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "986de458-22fe-36a5-be08-ba98cb6f5c9c",
                                        "entry_id": "3891231e-7325-3956-8fee-bb4c83854408",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To construct something, such as clothing, using the same technique."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8e22b7ec-f6e3-46c2-96de-1a7da681e1df",
                                                "sense_id": "986de458-22fe-36a5-be08-ba98cb6f5c9c",
                                                "text": "Get up, get up for shame, the blooming morne / Upon her wings presents the god unshorne. / See how Aurora throwes her faire / Fresh-quilted colours through the aire; / Get up, sweet slug-a-bed, and see / The dew bespangling herbe and tree."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "20476f22-4f2c-4d01-98a1-53bfe19c9fd4",
                                                "sense_id": "986de458-22fe-36a5-be08-ba98cb6f5c9c",
                                                "text": "Two hundred Sempſtreſſes were employed to make me Shirts, and Linen for Bed and Table, all of the ſtrongeft and coarſeſt kind they could get; which, however, they were forced to quilt together in ſeveral Folds, for the thickeſt was ſome degrees finer than Lawn."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a0d88437-a338-3f68-bf0f-e997515973d2",
                                        "entry_id": "3891231e-7325-3956-8fee-bb4c83854408",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To beat or thrash."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "625647ed-151b-4e05-8a62-e6fff8c322f8",
                                                "sense_id": "a0d88437-a338-3f68-bf0f-e997515973d2",
                                                "text": "I am glad, said Mr. Slick, that cussed critter, that schoolmaster, hasn't yet woke up. I'm most afeerd if he had aturned out afore we started, I should have quilted him, for that talk of his last night sticks in my crop considerable hard."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
